  "note": "Fortification works of the patchwork emplacement style, destroyed state, look 'derelict-pirate': every piece a lot's walls, parapets and barricades are drawn from, painted in ONE ImageGen pass over art-source/fortworks/guides/works-guide.png (make_guide.py) with the style's turret plinth as material reference, then edited into its destroyed state with the intact raw as edit target; prompt art-source/fortworks/prompts/derelict-pirate-destroyed.prompt.txt, raw retained unmodified. Cuts are measured from the intact raw (make_doc.py). Every id is a look <base id>@patchwork of a piece the generators lay: FortWorks dresses a piece on a lot built in this style with it, art only, so cover and blocking stay the base piece's (fort-works.md). One ring piece serves both barricade families.",
